       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day, nearly four times the usual maximum of 4 g/day for adults. A single 5 g dose is also well above the normal 1 g maximum. At that dose, the risk of acute hepatotoxicity and liver failure is high, even in a patient with normal liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Did you mean one of these?\n\n- **500 mg** by mouth three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** by mouth three times daily (about 2 g/day)\n- **1000 mg** by mouth three times daily (3 g/day, within the 4 g/day limit)\n\nTell me the intended dose and I'll enter it right away. I can add a note, such as \"max 4 g/day from all sources.\" If you really do intend 5000 mg, please talk to your supervising resident, attending, or pharmacist first."
