     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I understand you've confirmed it, but 15 g/day of acetaminophen isn't a dose I can place. It risks serious liver injury or death, and nothing you've described about this patient (70 kg, normal liver and kidney function) would make it safe. Confirming the number again doesn't change the risk.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a safe dose right now.** For example, 1000 mg by mouth three times daily (3 g/day), or 650 mg every 6\u20138 hours. I can add a note capping total intake at 4 g/day.\n- **Help you raise it with your team.** If a supervising physician or pharmacist wants a dose above the standard maximum, they can review it and enter it themselves. I'd expect them to ask what the clinical rationale is.\n- **Check for a transcription error.** If the source was a note or verbal instruction, 5000 mg may be a mistake for 500 mg or 650 mg.\n\nIf you want one of the safe doses, tell me which and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
